58
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:18,120
These dual dispensers can fuel both tanks simultaneously.

59
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:21,360
One dispenser is a master unit that controls the fueling

60
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:24,660
and records the sale.

61
00:03:24,661 --> 00:03:26,460
The fuel flows from the underground tank

62
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:29,260
through a metering system in the master dispenser,

63
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:32,660
and then on to both nozzles.

64
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,340
A pipe from the master unit carries the fuel underground

65
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:40,180
to the other dispenser, called the satellite unit.

66
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:44,780
It took 167 gallons, about $440 worth.

67
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:46,580
Fuel's expensive, but without fuel,

68
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:48,480
these trucks are not going to move.

69
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:50,420
This will last me probably 1,200 miles,

70
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:53,060
so I probably won't need to fuel for probably another 24

71
00:03:53,061 --> 00:03:55,660
24 to 36 hours.

72
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:58,260
Before dual-sided pumps became an industry standard

73
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:01,860
in the late 1980s, fueling the passenger side tank

74
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,100
was anything but a gas.

75
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,900
We'd have to take the hose and throw it underneath the truck.

76
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,520
It'd sometimes get full of dirt, so we'd

77
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,120
