109
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,540
finds a parking spot to let it air dry.

110
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,740
Iowa 80 has come a long way since it opened in 1964.

111
00:05:43,741 --> 00:05:48,740
1964.

112
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:52,040
Bill Moon, a regional manager for Standard Oil,

113
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:54,980
selected the site for his company.

114
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:57,580
It was strategically located along the emerging Interstate

115
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:00,180
80.

116
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:04,000
I-80 was to stretch from San Francisco almost 3,000 miles

117
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,400
east across the country to become one of America's first

118
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:11,940
interstate routes, a critical artery spanning all the way to

119
00:06:11,941 --> 00:06:15,140
in New York City.

120
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:18,680
When IO80 opened, however, traffic was light,

121
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:22,280
and so was the demand for truck stops.

122
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:25,280
We started out, and we had maybe two gas pumps

123
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:27,280
and about three diesel pumps.

124
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:31,100
We had a small store and parking for maybe eight or 10 trucks,

125
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:33,300
and that was it.

126
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,940
In 1984, Moon purchased the truck stop

127
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:38,600
