527
00:28:32,420 --> 00:28:33,700
And that's where the diesel is.

528
00:28:33,800 --> 00:28:37,160
That's where the trucker's entrance is.

529
00:28:37,260 --> 00:28:39,160
And that world is where the truck itself

530
00:28:39,260 --> 00:28:41,700
goes to the doctor.

531
00:28:41,701 --> 00:28:43,700
As a leading truck service provider,

532
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:47,140
TAs come equipped with computer diagnostics.

533
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:49,940
Their technicians can plug into the truck's onboard system

534
00:28:50,040 --> 00:28:52,940
to pinpoint problems.

535
00:28:53,040 --> 00:28:55,040
If the driver is complaining that something

536
00:28:55,140 --> 00:28:57,040
is wrong with the truck, I can click on fault codes

537
00:28:57,140 --> 00:28:59,360
and see if there's any fault codes coming up.

538
00:28:59,460 --> 00:29:03,860
There is a ECU, which is the Engine Control Unit, 128,

539
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:06,860
and it's a PID, and it's a parameter identifier,

540
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:11,700
and the ID is 111, and it's coolant level.

541
00:29:11,701 --> 00:29:13,440
The technology has advanced so much,

542
00:29:13,540 --> 00:29:15,940
the technicians can actually take control of the truck

543
00:29:16,040 --> 00:29:17,740
with their PCs.

544
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:19,800
What I'm going to do now is I'm going to click on the bulkhead

545
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:20,800
module.

546
00:29:20,900 --> 00:29:24,140
The bulkhead module is the brains of the truck.

547
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:27,640
A click of the mouse can operate the windshield wipers.

548
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:30,460
And you can see the wipers are working on low.

549
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:34,160
And it's also giving me an amp output as to how much amperage

550
00:29:34,260 --> 00:29:35,260
is drawing.

551
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:38,000
If the amperage is too much, I could see it on the screen,

552
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:40,460
indicating there's a problem.

553
00:29:40,461 --> 00:29:43,900
With innovative tech like this available at truck stops,

554
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:49,840
drivers can get a quick fix on their rig and keep on rolling.

555
00:29:49,940 --> 00:29:52,940
Back on the open road, however, highway checkpoints

556
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:57,480
can bring these metal behemoths to a halt.

557
00:29:57,580 --> 00:29:59,520
But new technology is allowing drivers

558
00:29:59,620 --> 00:30:03,480
to keep their 18 wheels turning with inspections on the fly.

559
00:30:03,481 --> 00:30:10,280
In 1968, the United States had about 2,000 truck stops.

560
00:30:10,380 --> 00:30:14,120
By 1972, more than 3,800.

561
00:30:14,220 --> 00:30:18,320
And today, there are more than 6,000 US truck stops.

562
00:30:18,420 --> 00:30:23,140
Truck stops will return on Modern Marvels.

563
00:30:30,540 --> 00:30:32,840
This big boy needs to weigh in.

564
00:30:32,841 --> 00:30:35,740
And he can do that right at the truck stop.

565
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:38,140
Hello?

566
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:39,440
Welcome, my lady.

567
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:40,640
Is this your first way?

568
00:30:40,740 --> 00:30:42,580
Yes, it is.

569
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:43,980
What's your truck number?

570
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:45,880
10-58.

571
00:30:45,980 --> 00:30:47,880
In just a fraction of a second,

572
00:30:47,980 --> 00:30:51,700
the automated scale calculates the weight of the heavy hauler.

573
00:30:51,800 --> 00:30:54,200
I have you, Wade, bring your trailer number in with you.

574
00:30:54,300 --> 00:30:55,700
Thanks.

575
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:57,640
The federal maximum weight allowed

576
00:30:57,740 --> 00:31:01,540
for a tractor and trailer is 80,000 pounds.

577
00:31:01,541 --> 00:31:04,740
And drivers rely on scales at truck stops to keep their weight

578
00:31:04,840 --> 00:31:07,140
in check.

579
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:09,640
Overweight trucks not only damage roads,

580
00:31:09,740 --> 00:31:12,280
but also pose grave dangers.

581
00:31:12,380 --> 00:31:15,280
The heavier the truck, the greater the distance and time

582
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:16,380
it needs to stop.

583
00:31:19,900 --> 00:31:23,700
A 100,000-pound truck takes 25% longer to stop

584
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:27,100
than an 80,000-pound truck.

585
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:29,900
Weigh stations along the highway ensure trucks

586
00:31:29,901 --> 00:31:32,140
trucks are within the legal limit.

587
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:34,900
It's very important that we be here

588
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:38,140
to be sure that weight is regulated properly.

589
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:41,980
Any time that one of these tractor and trailers

590
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:46,020
encounter a regular passenger vehicle,

591
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:48,960
of course, the passenger vehicle is going to lose,

592
00:31:49,060 --> 00:31:50,580
no matter who is at fault.

593
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:57,520
In 1913, Maine passed America's first law

594
00:31:57,620 --> 00:31:59,900
regulating truck weight.

595
00:31:59,901 --> 00:32:06,680
And by 1933, all states had some kind of truck weight limit.

596
00:32:06,780 --> 00:32:10,440
Modern truck scales consist of concrete and steel plates

597
00:32:10,540 --> 00:32:13,740
that rest on a set of load cells.

598
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:18,560
A load cell converts force into a measurable electrical output.

599
00:32:18,660 --> 00:32:21,760
A load cell looks exactly like this.

600
00:32:21,860 --> 00:32:25,560
Inside the cell, you can see a stainless steel bar down

601
00:32:25,660 --> 00:32:26,460
the middle.

602
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:29,060
Attached to it are strain gauges.

603
00:32:29,061 --> 00:32:30,860
What actually is measured by this cell

604
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:34,760
is the compression of this stainless steel rod.

605
00:32:34,860 --> 00:32:37,200
As the truck drives onto the scale,

606
00:32:37,300 --> 00:32:41,300
the load cells compress, causing the strain gauges to deform

607
00:32:41,400 --> 00:32:45,100
and generate a change in voltage.

608
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:47,620
This electrical signal is sent from each load cell

609
00:32:47,720 --> 00:32:50,620
through a device called a sectional controller

610
00:32:50,720 --> 00:32:53,520
and into the fuel center, where a computer digitally

611
00:32:53,620 --> 00:32:54,820
calculates the weight of the truck.

612
00:32:54,821 --> 00:33:01,320
The science of weighing heavy objects dates back to 200 BC,

613
00:33:01,420 --> 00:33:05,060
when the Romans invented the steel yard.

614
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:10,060
They used it to weigh precious goods, like gold.

615
00:33:10,160 --> 00:33:13,400
The steel yard consisted of a beam with a sliding weight

616
00:33:13,500 --> 00:33:16,000
to counterbalance the load.

617
00:33:16,100 --> 00:33:17,940
Today, this type of device is still

618
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:20,840
used in the modern scales at most doctor's offices.

619
00:33:20,841 --> 00:33:26,780
How about a doctor scale three stories high?

620
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:30,080
These massive steel yards were developed in the 18th century

621
00:33:30,180 --> 00:33:32,780
to weigh wagons and rail cars.

622
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:36,660
Commerce pushed the weighing of heavy items in the 1800s,

623
00:33:36,760 --> 00:33:40,120
just as if you would have a farm and you were hauling some type

624
00:33:40,220 --> 00:33:43,160
of produce, you would want to weigh that produce when you

625
00:33:43,260 --> 00:33:45,660
would buy it in bulk.

626
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:49,000
But using steel yards was a daunting task

627
00:33:49,001 --> 00:33:53,000
because the vehicles had to be lifted up onto the scale.

628
00:33:53,100 --> 00:33:55,700
Innovators tried to devise an easier method

629
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:58,740
and succeeded with the platform scale.

630
00:33:58,840 --> 00:34:02,040
In the 1830s, a gentleman named Thaddeus Fairbanks

631
00:34:02,140 --> 00:34:04,440
patented the first platform scale.

632
00:34:04,540 --> 00:34:06,660
Now something such as a horse-drawn cart

633
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:09,960
could be pulled directly onto the scale.

634
00:34:10,060 --> 00:34:11,760
The platform scale incorporated

635
00:34:11,860 --> 00:34:13,500
the principles of the steel yard,

636
00:34:13,600 --> 00:34:17,560
with two levers supporting a platform.

637
00:34:17,561 --> 00:34:19,360
Pivot points at each corner of the scale

638
00:34:19,460 --> 00:34:24,340
allowed the force of the load to be transferred to both levers.

639
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:26,700
The central lever pulled down on the steel yard

640
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:30,300
that determined the weight of the load.

641
00:34:30,400 --> 00:34:33,080
In the late 1940s, the platform scale

642
00:34:33,180 --> 00:34:36,080
incorporated electronics.

643
00:34:36,180 --> 00:34:40,680
And today, load cells dominate the weighing industry.

644
00:34:40,780 --> 00:34:43,860
But the laborious process of stopping the weigh-in

645
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:47,560
is slowing truck traffic.

646
00:34:47,561 --> 00:34:50,300
Especially since the number of big rigs on the road is

647
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:54,900
skyrocketing, up more than 30% since 1993.

648
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,900
This may be the answer to a trucker's prayers.

649
00:35:04,720 --> 00:35:07,920
The Oak Ridge National Lab in Oak Ridge, Tennessee,

650
00:35:08,020 --> 00:35:11,220
has integrated weigh-in motion technology and other sensor

651
00:35:11,320 --> 00:35:15,160
technologies to speed up the process.

652
00:35:15,161 --> 00:35:18,060
The system was first installed in 1995

653
00:35:18,160 --> 00:35:20,300
at the nation's second busiest weigh station

654
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:22,800
in Tennessee's Knox County.

655
00:35:22,900 --> 00:35:24,700
This is a weigh-in motion system.

656
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:28,400
It's basically a metal plate that is laying on a load cell,

657
00:35:28,500 --> 00:35:31,200
and it can detect the weight of the truck

658
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:33,520
at pretty high speeds.

659
00:35:33,620 --> 00:35:35,220
Similar to the static scale,

660
00:35:35,320 --> 00:35:38,520
load cells capture the instantaneous force one axle

661
00:35:38,620 --> 00:35:41,620
at a time as the truck drives over them.

662
00:35:41,621 --> 00:35:44,860
Our drivers never have to stop to weigh in.

663
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:49,260
They can just roll right over the scale at 30 miles per hour.

664
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:51,960
And only those trucks that are within 2,000 pounds

665
00:35:52,060 --> 00:35:54,960
of the legal limit or exceeded are pulled in

666
00:35:55,060 --> 00:35:57,860
for a more precise calculation.

667
00:35:57,960 --> 00:35:59,480
As he's coming up through there,

668
00:35:59,580 --> 00:36:01,280
you can see he's got a good tag.

669
00:36:01,380 --> 00:36:03,180
The driver does have his seat belt on,

670
00:36:03,280 --> 00:36:05,180
company name's on the side of the truck.

671
00:36:05,280 --> 00:36:07,980
His DOT number's there and his fuel permit.

672
00:36:08,080 --> 00:36:09,580
Tires all look good.

673
00:36:09,680 --> 00:36:11,080
We'll look down and check his weight.

674
00:36:11,081 --> 00:36:13,480
his weight looks good, so then I'll release him.

675
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:19,520
Just 85 miles north at the Laurel County, Kentucky

676
00:36:19,620 --> 00:36:22,820
weigh station, Oak Ridge National Lab and Kentucky

677
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:25,520
Vehicle Enforcement have deployed another advanced

678
00:36:25,620 --> 00:36:31,340
system that can both weigh and inspect the truck in motion.

679
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:33,740
It even sniffs for bombs.

680
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:36,440
So essentially what we're doing is placing the proper sensors

681
00:36:36,540 --> 00:36:39,480
out here, information that we can attain off of a truck in

682
00:36:39,481 --> 00:36:42,980
in motion and provide that in a near instantaneous manner

683
00:36:42,981 --> 00:36:46,320
to the state police.

684
00:36:46,321 --> 00:36:48,160
As the truck pulls into the station,

685
00:36:48,161 --> 00:36:51,500
it travels over a weigh-in motion scale.

686
00:36:51,501 --> 00:36:54,920
Then it passes an infrared camera that checks the brakes.

687
00:36:54,921 --> 00:36:57,500
An infrared camera only sees heat.

688
00:36:57,501 --> 00:37:02,440
So heat is displayed as white and cold as black.

689
00:37:02,441 --> 00:37:06,000
Brakes work by producing heat from motion energy.

690
00:37:06,001 --> 00:37:09,840
So if there is no heat, there is no brake.

691
00:37:09,940 --> 00:37:13,200
This is a laser scanner that collects information

692
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:15,040
about the overall length of the truck,

693
00:37:15,140 --> 00:37:17,940
how many axles the truck has, and the speed of the truck.

694
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:19,940
This is a radiation detector.

695
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:22,820
The radiation detector measures for gamma and neutron

696
00:37:22,920 --> 00:37:25,120
radiation.

697
00:37:25,220 --> 00:37:26,680
The radiation portal monitor

698
00:37:26,780 --> 00:37:29,320
can detect trace amounts of threat substances based

699
00:37:29,420 --> 00:37:33,120
on their radiation signature, all while the truck is in motion.

700
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:38,000
This device can help prevent terrorists

701
00:37:38,100 --> 00:37:40,900
from transporting dirty bombs and biological warfare

702
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:44,240
agents across the country.

703
00:37:44,340 --> 00:37:47,140
This is an automatic license plate recognition system.

704
00:37:47,240 --> 00:37:50,440
It actually takes a pretty wide view of the front of the truck,

705
00:37:50,540 --> 00:37:52,760
finds the license plate, zooms in on it,

706
00:37:52,860 --> 00:37:54,980
takes the text from the front of it,

707
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:58,260
and sends it to a database to be checked.

708
00:37:58,360 --> 00:38:00,160
In a matter of seconds, the station

709
00:38:00,260 --> 00:38:02,860
gathers enough information to give the truck a green light

710
00:38:02,861 --> 00:38:07,560
light to exit or a red light to pull up for inspection.

711
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:11,200
A weigh station can not only be a place that we do road

712
00:38:11,300 --> 00:38:13,800
preservation and highway safety, but it can help us from the

713
00:38:13,900 --> 00:38:16,900
standpoint of homeland security, environmental protection, and

714
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:19,300
highway congestion.

715
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:23,420
Less congestion means less wasted diesel fuel.

716
00:38:23,520 --> 00:38:25,820
And one country music legend's truck stop

717
00:38:25,920 --> 00:38:29,660
venture may even get rigs back on the road again without relying

718
00:38:29,760 --> 00:38:32,520
on imported oil.

719
00:38:32,521 --> 00:38:36,520
The trucker's term for a weigh station is chicken coop.

720
00:38:36,620 --> 00:38:39,320
Rest areas are called nap traps, and the truck stop

721
00:38:39,420 --> 00:38:41,620
is known as the water hole.

722
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:44,460
Truck stops will return on Modern Marvels.

723
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:53,380
Truckers traveling down Interstate 35 between Dallas

724
00:38:53,480 --> 00:38:57,580
and Waco, Texas seek out one of the most unique truck stops

725
00:38:57,680 --> 00:39:00,280
in the United States.

726
00:39:00,281 --> 00:39:03,520
Two things make Carl's Corner unusual.

727
00:39:03,620 --> 00:39:07,520
It's co-owned by country music legend Willie Nelson.

728
00:39:07,620 --> 00:39:11,520
And the fuel sold here, Bio Willie, is a biofuel.

729
00:39:11,620 --> 00:39:16,220
It's 80% diesel and 20% vegetable oil.

730
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:19,560
This clean-burning biodiesel blend reduces harmful exhaust

731
00:39:19,660 --> 00:39:22,640
emissions by more than 10%.

732
00:39:22,740 --> 00:39:25,840
And that's not the only advantage it offers.

733
00:39:25,940 --> 00:39:29,580
Well, the truckers tell me they do get better gas mileage.

734
00:39:29,581 --> 00:39:32,480
and that means more money in their pocket.

735
00:39:32,580 --> 00:39:37,480
So naturally, this perks up their ears a little bit.

736
00:39:37,580 --> 00:39:39,820
Biodiesel is made through a chemical process

737
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:42,860
called transesterification, in which glycerin

738
00:39:42,960 --> 00:39:45,360
is separated from oil through the use of a catalyst

739
00:39:45,460 --> 00:39:48,260
and an alcohol.

740
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:50,260
We're going to make some biodiesel here.

741
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:53,240
So I've got a beaker of vegetable oil.

742
00:39:53,340 --> 00:39:54,840
We're going to put it on a stir plate,

743
00:39:54,841 --> 00:40:01,840
plate and I'm going to add in my alcohol and catalyst mixture here.

744
00:40:01,841 --> 00:40:04,840
And let's see what happens.

745
00:40:10,840 --> 00:40:16,840
You can see the oil got murky as it started to, the glycerin is starting to break from the biodiesel.

746
00:40:16,841 --> 00:40:21,140
And now it's turned a nice clear color, which means that most

747
00:40:21,240 --> 00:40:26,280
of the glycerin has separated from the methyl ester chains.

748
00:40:26,380 --> 00:40:32,820
And that's basically biodiesel right there.

749
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:34,320
During the chemical reaction,

750
00:40:34,420 --> 00:40:36,960
the methanol molecule is attached to the fatty acid

751
00:40:37,060 --> 00:40:39,700
chain of vegetable oil.

752
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:41,940
The three bonds of the glycerol molecule

753
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:43,960
break off due to this interaction,

754
00:40:43,961 --> 00:40:48,860
resulting in three long methyl ester chains, or biodiesel.

755
00:40:52,160 --> 00:40:56,040
Carl's Corner sets itself apart not only by selling biodiesel,

756
00:40:56,140 --> 00:40:59,480
but also by producing it right at the truck stop.

757
00:40:59,580 --> 00:41:03,440
A newly constructed facility refines 8,000 gallons every day.

758
00:41:05,980 --> 00:41:08,660
Every unit of fossil fuel required to make biodiesel

759
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:12,660
results in 3.2 units of energy gain.

760
00:41:12,661 --> 00:41:17,460
On the downside, biodiesel can gel in cold weather.

761
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:20,700
So how did a brand of biodiesel named after a country music

762
00:41:20,800 --> 00:41:24,000
star get its start here?

763
00:41:24,100 --> 00:41:26,500
Let's go back to 1979.

764
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:30,820
That's when a friend of Willie's, entrepreneur Carl Cornelius,

765
00:41:30,920 --> 00:41:35,520
opened Carl's Corner to fill the needs of passing truckers.

766
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:38,020
I started one room at a time.

767
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:40,560
And if they asked for a swimming pool, I put it in.

768
00:41:40,561 --> 00:41:41,400
I put it in.

769
00:41:41,401 --> 00:41:42,760
They asked for a hot tub, put it in.

770
00:41:42,761 --> 00:41:46,760
They asked for an adult bar, I put it in.

